# Line endings.
#
# styles/ IS HASH-PINNED, so its bytes must be identical on every platform.
# styles/Taste/STYLE_SOURCE.json records a SHA-256 per vendored rule. Without an
# eol rule Git checks those files out with CRLF on Windows and LF elsewhere, so
# the digests describe bytes that exist on one runner and not the other. Measured:
# PR #197 passed `validator (ubuntu-latest)` and failed `validator (windows-latest)`
# with all six digests mismatched and nothing wrong with the files.
#
# A hash over a text file must not depend on the platform that checked it out.
styles/** text eol=lf

# The sibling measurement repository pins the same way; matching it keeps a
# vendored file byte-equal across the boundary it is vendored over.
*.py text eol=lf
*.md text eol=lf
*.yml text eol=lf
*.yaml text eol=lf
*.json text eol=lf
*.sh text eol=lf
*.ini text eol=lf

# PowerShell is the deliberate exception: the Windows host that runs it expects CRLF.
*.ps1 text eol=crlf
